# Client-side API only

This project must behave as a client-side frontend for backend API integration.

## Requirements

- Do not create new API handlers under `src/app/api/**`.
- Do not route frontend API calls through Next.js server routes as a proxy/bff layer.
- Call backend APIs directly from client-side code, shared client utilities, or feature services.
- Keep business/data-fetching logic in reusable modules (for example under `src/lib/**`) that are safe for client usage.

## Existing legacy routes

- Existing files under `src/app/api/**` are considered legacy and should not be expanded.
- If touching an area that still depends on legacy routes, prefer migrating usage toward direct backend calls.

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ Not allowed: frontend -> /api/* (Next.js route)
await fetch("/api/auth/login", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(payload) });

// ✅ Preferred: frontend -> backend endpoint directly
await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_API_URL}/dog-owner/login`, {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify(payload),
});
```
